Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
>
> A while ago, while reviewing my causes of death on NAO, I noticed that
> I had a couple of deaths to mimics in very early shops.  Since then
> I've been more careful about shops in the extremely early game (I
> still use them to price-check items I'm carrying, but I don't usually
> check the shop's inventory), but here's my question:  approximately
> how *long* do I need to wait, to be relatively sure that shop use
> won't be fatal?  Mimics aren't particularly dangerous a little later
> in the game, but how _much_ later are we talking?  How many hitpoints,
> and what level of equipment and/or experience, would adequately
> prepare me to take out an early mimic without weakening myself
> dangerously?

There are ways to tell which squares in a shop are mimics and which
squares are items.  If you never move onto a mimic you never attack it
and it never attacks you.  Of course even one typo is enough to move
onto a mimic's square and start the combat.

If you kill roughly the same number of monsters as your pet, you're
roughly as powerful as your pet.  If your pet attacks a mimic in that
case you can fight it as a team and kill it.

I thought a good MC#3 cloak reduced a mimic's ability to grab you.  Not
sure if that's wrong.  The problem is by the time my characters have a
good MC#3 cloak they can fight and kill mimics.  That does answer the
original question indirectly.  If you've killed enough elves to have an
elven cloak you're ready.  If you've been to mines end you're ready.


